lang.org/ |access-date=17 August 2025 |website=mypy-lang.org}} {{As of|2026}}, the [[Python Software Foundation]] supports Python 3.15.2, 3.14.10, 3.13.18, 3.12.16 and 3.11.18 that all were "expedited security releases" in October 2026, following the project's annual release cycle and five-year support policy. Python 3.15 the latest stable release defaults to [[UTF-8]], unlike previous versions. Earlier versions in the 3.x series have reached end-of-life and no longer receive security updates. Python is widely taught as an introductory programming language.{{Cite journal |last1=Sultana |first1=Simon G. |last2=Reed |first2=Philip A. |date=2017 |title=Curriculum for an Introductory Computer Science Course: Identifying Recommendations from Academia and Industry |journal=The Journal of Technology Studies |volume=43 |issue=2 |pages=80– 92 |doi=10.21061/jots.v43i2.a.3 |issn=1071-6084 |jstor=90023144}}
